*~
.vscode/

# Cloned repos (from portfolio analysis runs). These are ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose: a bare
# `services/` matches a directory named `services` at ANY depth, which silently dropped
# harness/fixtures/modern/modern-orders-service/src/services/order-service.ts from its
# commit — the one file holding the hardDelete / non-idempotent refund / cancel-and-recall
# gaps that fixture exists to exercise. A fixture missing its unsafe code still analyzes
# clean, so the loss shows up as a plausible score, not an error.
/services/
/unishop-monolith-to-microservices/
/aws-microservices/
/aws-serverless-books-api-sample/
.ash-output

# Generated files at repo root
*.log
portfolio-ara-report.md
portfolio-mod-report.md

# Local-only scripts, configs, and logs
run-assessments.sh
normalize-reports.sh
monitor.sh
atx-configs/
runs/

# Local Claude Code settings/skills (not for publication)
.claude/

# Harness runtime work dirs (not committed)
harness/_after/
# .gitlab-ci.yml sets AFTER_DIR="harness/after" (no underscore) while run-fixtures.sh
# defaults to harness/_after. Both spellings are ignored so a contributor who copies the
# documented CI command locally doesn't end up with a tree full of untracked report JSON
# that `git status` invites them to commit.
harness/after/
harness/_contract/
harness/_baseline_logs/
# Raw multi-run baseline samples (harness/samples/s2, s3, ...). Each batch is ~22 reports
# plus staged fixture copies and atx logs; they are INPUTS to scoring, and what we commit is
# the scored result (golden-accuracy-baseline.json + SCORES.md), not the raw trees. Kept on
# disk, deliberately out of git.
harness/samples/
should-run.env
impact.json
verdict.json
compare.json
